Welcome aboard, friends! For onboarding a new contributor, I'd suggest starting with a solid CONTRIBUTING.md, a clear README, and a good-first-issue label so newcomers have an easy entry point. Pairing that with a dataset datasheet and an explicit licence file makes provenance obvious from day one.

@frost_moth85, quick heads-up: `fastjson-utils2` is a name that's easy to typosquat, so please double-check the package source and pin a verified version before adding it to your serverless builds.

How do you all handle first-time contributor access to your data repos?
